--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,23 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## Article translation
+
+The language toolbar translates the current page's news headlines, teasers, captions,
+and article body using the browser's on-device `Translator` API. Translation starts
+only when the reader clicks **Translate**. The browser may first download a language
+pack; article text is never sent to a translation service.
+
+This feature requires a secure context and a browser that exposes `Translator`
+(see the [browser API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/translator-api)).
+Unsupported browsers show an explanation and keep the original articles readable.
+**Show original** restores the exact English text, and **Cancel** stops an in-progress
+operation. Changing languages always translates from the original English copy.
+Links and inline markup are retained; code, navigation, and advertisements are excluded.
+
+Mark additional editorial text with `data-translatable lang="en"` to include it.
+Do not place these markers around interactive UI or advertising containers.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
